Source: @SOURCE_PACKAGE@
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               cmake (>= 3.25),
               ninja-build,
               pkgconf,
               libssl-dev (>= 3.0.0)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: @HOMEPAGE@
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: @RUNTIME_PACKAGE@
Architecture: any
Depends: @LIB_PACKAGE@ (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: paired reader/writer key-value storage daemon
 GlifiStore is an architectural prototype of a key-value store built on paired
 Reader-Writer shards, partition ownership, immutable read generations and
 fail-closed recovery. It speaks wire protocol v2 and writes persistence
 format v1.
 .
 This package installs the glifistored daemon, the operator tools
 (verify, repair, backup, migrate, rebuild-index, inspect-segment), the manuals
 and a systemd unit. The unit is installed but neither enabled nor started: the
 shipped configuration binds the loopback interface and every limit has to be
 reviewed before non-loopback use.
 .
 The project publishes no production-readiness, durability-certification or
 hostile-deployment claim.

Package: @LIB_PACKAGE@
Architecture: any
Section: libs
Multi-Arch: no
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: GlifiStore C ABI shared library
 Runtime shared library exposing the stable GlifiStore C ABI, versioned by the
 ABI_VERSION authority of the source tree rather than by the product version.
 .
 The package is deliberately not Multi-Arch: same. The installed pkg-config file
 derives its prefix from its own location two levels up, which only holds while
 the library lives in a non-multiarch libdir.

Package: @DEV_PACKAGE@
Architecture: any
Section: libdevel
Depends: @LIB_PACKAGE@ (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: GlifiStore development files
 Headers, static libraries, the pkg-config file and the CMake package
 configuration needed to build an external consumer against an installed
 GlifiStore.
